  "term": "sensory cue",
  "definition": "A sensory cue is a detectable feature of the environment that an organism uses to guide perception or behavior, such as orienting in a particular direction. In this source, the Earth’s geomagnetic field is described as a possible sensory cue for navigation toward food.",
